            "text": "{\"description\":\"The main stone surface shows a tall carved figure-like form with a smaller upper portion and broad lower front. On the lower front there are two deep circular depressions, a central raised circular disk, curving parallel bands below it, and shallow curved/linear incisions around them. The upper visible surface is worn and includes vertical and curved carved lines, but many details are indistinct.\",\"avian\":{\"answer\":\"absent\",\"evidence\":\"No clearly carved bird body or birdlike head/beak is visible on the main stone surface; birdlike shapes in the background are ignored.\",\"box\":null},\"large_face\":{\"answer\":\"uncertain\",\"evidence\":\"The broad lower area has two round depressions and a central round disk that could be read as facial features, but they are not clearly a human face and the surface is very worn.\",\"box\":null},\"scorpion\":{\"answer\":\"absent\",\"evidence\":\"I do not see a carved scorpion with legs or a segmented upturned tail on the stone surface.\",\"box\":null},\"round_motif\":{\"answer\":\"present\",\"evidence\":\"A distinct raised circular motif is visible near the center of the lower front surface, separate from the two deep depressions.\",\"box\":[0.385,0.535,0.572,0.651]},\"three_arches\":{\"answer\":\"absent\",\"evidence\":\"There are curved parallel bands, but not three arch-topped forms arranged side by side in a row.\",\"box\":null},\"limitations\":\"The stone is dark, rough, and heavily worn; lighting and shadow obscure shallow incisions, and some carvings are ambiguous.\"}",
